   "speech": "The fundamental tone of Duplay’s life was a sense of musical enchantment that never left him. The best example of this, one that fully explains such a peculiarity of soul, may be found in the cinematograph, whose pictures, as is well known, are accompanied by music. Silent action, coloured by the sounds of fitting melodies, acquires a poetic hue. Moral perspective is lost: heroism and debauchery, benediction and villainy, while producing different impressions upon the eye, yield in their sum only an absorbing spectacle — the feelings are stirred, but stirred aesthetically. Between the action and the orchestra there spreads the invisible shadow of an elegy, and in that shadow the boundaries of facts are drowned, making of them — let us repeat it — an absorbing spectacle. The cause is musical enchantment; the effect is a play of moved feelings, leading through the shadow of an elegy to the joy of heightened contemplation.",
